  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 151 AM CDT Sun Aug 30 2026\n\nA broad ridge continues to dominate the weather across the central \nCONUS tonight and this feature is expected to remain in place \nthrough the next 7-10 days with little or no reprieve. This is \nexpected to result in much above normal temperatures (record highs \nat times) with minimal chances for wetting precipitation over the \nupcoming week.\n\nDaily highs may peak today in the 102-106 range today while\nremaining above the century mark through the next 7 days \nalthough a subtle decrease in air temperature may occur by Tue-\nWed as the upper ridge translates slightly eastward and some \nincrease in low level moisture over parts of eastern Kansas. We \nare basically expecting a persistence forecast through the \nupcoming week with only subtle changes from day-to-day.",
